>> title: Ciabatta
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, italian, yeast, biga, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Deli
>> servings: 10
>> time: 16 hr
>> slack: narrow — the folds are on a timer, every thirty minutes for two hours, and this dough is too slack to survive being handled late; after the cut it gets forty-five minutes and no more, because a slack dough that over-proofs spreads flat on the peel and never comes back up
>> step.1: stir the biga, rest 12 hours
>> step.2: mix to a slack dough
>> step.3: fold in the bowl every 30 min for 2 hours
>> step.4: cut in two on a dusted peel, rest 45 min
>> step.5: bake 475°F 22 min with steam

Stir @bread flour{1 1/2%cup}(200 g), @cool water{1/2%cup}(115 g), and @instant yeast{1/8%tsp}(0.4 g) to a stiff biga, then rest ~{12%hours}.

Mix @&(~1)biga{} with @bread flour{2 1/4%cup}(300 g), @warm water{1 1/4%cup}(285 g), @instant yeast{1%tsp}(3 g), and @fine sea salt{2%tsp}(10 g).

Fold @&(~1)dough{} in the bowl every ~{30%min} until puffed and airy.

Cut @&(~1)dough{} into two loaves on a #peel{} dusted with @semolina{2%Tbs}, then rest ~{45%min}.

Bake @&(~1)loaves{} at 475°F with steam for ~{22%min}.
